+## Voyage R6 — Browser DOM identity & editing visibility
+
+**Defects reported by external Cypress acceptance suite (10 failures):**
+
+1. **Failures 1-4 (DOM detachment):** `render()` clears `todoList.innerHTML = ''` and rebuilds every `<li>` from scratch on every state change (toggle, toggle-all). In a real browser, Cypress holds references to pre-click nodes; after `render()` destroys and recreates them, the references detach.
+   - **Fix required:** Mutate existing `<li>` nodes in-place (toggle class/checkbox) instead of rebuilding the list.
+
+2. **Failures 5-10 (Edit input not visible):** The dblclick handler sets `todo.editing = true`, then calls `render()`. `render()` starts with `todos = getTodos()` (re-reads from localStorage), discarding the transient `editing` flag. New `<li>` never gets `.editing` class, so `.edit` stays `display: none`.
+   - **Fix required:** Stop re-reading from localStorage at the top of `render()`; use the in-memory `todos` array so transient state persists across renders.
+
+Both share root cause: `render()` destroys and rebuilds DOM nodes instead of mutating in-place. Not reproducible in happy-dom harness (step definitions hack around both issues). Conformance scenarios added to fail on current source.
+
